{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report — repair commit aa2b7f418ca975840650ef0f598f46871ad3fafd\n\nProblem: malformed overlap candidate-id responses consumed multiple 16,000-token generations and multi-minute request windows before the advisory path abstained.\n\nProven root cause: judge_batch declared no operation-local output, structured-retry, transport-attempt, or timeout ceilings, so it inherited generic 16,000-token, three-generation, four-transport-attempt, 600-second policy. The Phase 1 RCA comment at 1786251659444495001 cites the original execution path and runtime traces. Closed story 9022-d3e3-e97f-47e3 and ADR 0086 establish the violated intent: the classifier is bounded and advisory, and timeout/error/malformed output must degrade promptly to abstention.\n\nProof: the real judge → PydanticAIRunner path made three 16,000-token generations before repair. A token-only mutation lowered max_tokens but still made three generations, ruling out output size as sufficient containment. Removing all four overlap-local limits after repair restored exactly three 16,000-token generations. Separate timeout and truncation mutations also restored RED.\n\nTest: tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py exercises malformed runaway output, truncation, timeout, one-transport-attempt declaration, exact all-candidate abstention, and a valid reversed six-candidate control. tests/unit/test_runner_hardening.py proves zero structured retries means one generation. tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py proves lower-only config behavior reaches model and provider construction. The held-out oracle was RED before repair, GREEN after repair, RED again under the defect-seeded mutation, then GREEN after restoration. It asserts observable settings/results and survives behavior-preserving refactors.\n\nFix: RunRequest now has defaulted lowering-only structured retry, transport attempt, and timeout seams (src/rebar/llm/runner.py:111-113). _effective_config applies timeout and transport ceilings before model/provider construction (runner.py:230-235). Both structured-output paths honor the request ceiling (src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:217-218 and its native/prompted consumers). judge_batch requests 1,024 output tokens, one structured generation, one transport attempt, and a 60-second timeout (src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py:181-184). Existing callers omit these fields and retain prior defaults.\n\nScope and safety: the caller sweep found judge_batch only behind judge at judge.py:284-285 and overlap_findings at wire.py:55; callers depend on advisory abstention, not runaway budgets. The repair restores documented containment, creates no new entry point or external effect, adds no dependency, and weakens no existing test. Resulting modules remain under the 800-line hard cap.\n\nSiblings/parity: no construct sibling was found; the missing limit was localized to this advisory operation. Channel census: the operation is internal to plan review through overlap_findings; CLI and automated plan review share that core. There is no direct MCP/API or public-library judge surface, and no dual-direction mirror. No MISSING parity surface remains.\n\nVerification: held-out focused suite 56 passed; broader affected-surface suite 267 passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed for 442 source files; git diff --check passed. The optional full default suite was stopped at 5 percent clean and is not claimed as passed. Local four-pass review-code at aa2b7f4 returned PASS with 0 blocking and 0 advisory findings.\n\nOriginal-path replication: an overlap-enabled review-plan --source local --no-sign --force reproduced the original runaway candidate-id failure mode. With the repair, malformed orderings stopped after one generation in 22.7s and 10.1s, with EOF payload columns 2,975 and 1,053, returned overlap: [], and fabricated no finding. Full review elapsed 202.96s, dominated by normal review passes rather than overlap retries.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: none observed beyond normal live-model variability; bounded abstention is now enforced by deterministic tests. Gerrit Verified remains authoritative for the full suite."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786257174035442001,"uuid":"faa40cb7-90bc-4f24-b6e3-2eaa6fe7de54"}